      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 4.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.56,
      "end_seconds": 10.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.7,
      "end_seconds": 20.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "mainly shaky spells in the afternoon there's a couple of other things, but that's the the main one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.07,
      "end_seconds": 23.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.36,
      "end_seconds": 33.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Since last night, that's when it began"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.23,
      "end_seconds": 38.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.65,
      "end_seconds": 40.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.08,
      "end_seconds": 46.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "let me check a few things any loss of consciousness or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.37,
      "end_seconds": 53.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "No loss of consciousness or chest pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.42,
      "end_seconds": 57.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Have you had any vomiting or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.55,
      "end_seconds": 63.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "no, um, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.61,
      "end_seconds": 65.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.59,
      "end_seconds": 70.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, uh, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.66,
      "end_seconds": 86.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.14,
      "end_seconds": 95.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. Iron tablets. I take it once a day for my blood count"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.88,
      "end_seconds": 100.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.7,
      "end_seconds": 113.74,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.88,
      "end_seconds": 119.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.65,
      "end_seconds": 121.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.66,
      "end_seconds": 123.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.86,
      "end_seconds": 128.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.05,
      "end_seconds": 131.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Yes. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.11,
      "end_seconds": 135.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Yeah, no, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.31,
      "end_seconds": 146.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.22,
      "end_seconds": 159.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.97,
      "end_seconds": 184.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.9 degrees, blood pressure 124 over 84, saturation 99 percent, pulse 114, height 165 centimetres, weight 53 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.74,
      "end_seconds": 190.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.1,
      "end_seconds": 193.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.54,
      "end_seconds": 209.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Your sugar reading in clinic is on the low side and your pulse is a little fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.02,
      "end_seconds": 219.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.79,
      "end_seconds": 237.73,
      "duration_seconds": 14.94,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards recurrent low blood sugar on insulin. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.26,
      "end_seconds": 242.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Erm, what are the the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.96,
      "end_seconds": 280.57,
      "duration_seconds": 36.61,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's recurrent low blood sugar on insulin, and we'll know more once the a download of the glucose meter is back. I think a download of the glucose meter makes sense here, for hypoglycaemia. The treatment will be insulin glargine, 16 units, once a day at bedtime, long term. It's for diabetes. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.56,
      "end_seconds": 285.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "always carry sugar and eat something before exercise"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.47,
      "end_seconds": 299.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.79,
      "text": "Ah. An HbA1c is something we might do if this doesn't improve in a month. I'd like you back in two weeks. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.55,
      "end_seconds": 303.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.24,
      "end_seconds": 306.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Right, goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}